# Architecture

## Overview

{{ project_name }} is a Python agent application using {{ agent_framework }}{% if execution_model != "cli" %} with a FastAPI backend{% endif %}.

## Project Structure

```
src/{{ package_name }}/
  agents/              # Agent definitions
    example.py         # Example agent ({{ agent_framework }})
  tools/               # Agent tools/functions
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
  cli.py               # Typer CLI entry point
  commands/            # CLI subcommands
{%- else %}
  app.py               # FastAPI app factory
  telemetry.py         # OpenTelemetry setup
  routers/             # HTTP endpoint definitions
    health.py          # /healthz, /readyz
  controllers/         # Request orchestration
  dtos/                # Pydantic request/response models
{%- endif %}
{%- if execution_model == "web" %}
  web/                 # Frontend integration
    serve.py           # Static file serving for production
    frontend/          # Frontend app (scaffolded separately)
{%- endif %}
  config.py            # Pydantic-settings config from env vars
  logging.py           # structlog setup
  services/            # Business logic
{%- if include_clients %}
  clients/             # External API/service clients
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
  db.py                # Async engine/session factory
  models/              # SQLAlchemy async models
  repositories/        # Data access layer
{%- endif %}
tests/
  unit/                # Fast, isolated unit tests
  integration/         # Tests with real dependencies
  e2e/                 # End-to-end tests
```
{% if execution_model == "cli" %}
## Flow

```
CLI commands (parse args, call agents)
  -> agents ({{ agent_framework }}, orchestrate tools)
    -> tools (functions the agent can call)
    -> services (business logic)
{%- if include_clients %}
      -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
      -> repositories (data access)
{%- endif %}
```
{% else %}
## Layering

```
routers (HTTP endpoints, parse requests into DTOs)
  -> controllers (orchestrate across services/agents)
    -> agents ({{ agent_framework }}, orchestrate tools)
      -> tools (functions the agent can call)
    -> services (business logic, framework-agnostic)
{%- if include_clients %}
      -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
      -> repositories (data access, return SQLAlchemy models)
        -> models (SQLAlchemy)
{%- endif %}
```

DTOs (Pydantic models) are used at the router and controller level for API I/O. They are always separate from database models.
{% endif %}
## Toolchain

| Tool | Purpose |
| ---- | ------- |
| uv | Package management, virtual environments |
| hatchling | Build backend |
| ruff | Formatting and linting |
| ty | Type checking |
| pytest | Testing |
| {{ agent_framework }} | Agent framework |
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
| typer | CLI framework |
{%- else %}
| FastAPI | Async web framework |
| uvicorn | ASGI server |
| OpenTelemetry | Distributed tracing |
{%- endif %}
| structlog | Structured logging |
| pydantic-settings | Configuration |
{%- if execution_model == "web" %}
| pnpm | Frontend package management |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
| SQLAlchemy | Async ORM |
| Alembic | Database migrations |
{%- endif %}

## Conventions

- All configuration is in `pyproject.toml`.
- Version is the single source of truth in `pyproject.toml`, read via `importlib.metadata`.
- `py.typed` marker enables downstream type checking (PEP 561).
{%- if execution_model != "cli" %}
- Health endpoints are always available at `/healthz` and `/readyz`.
{%- endif %}
{%- if execution_model == "web" %}
- Just targets have `-be`/`-fe` variants for backend/frontend.
{%- endif %}
